    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We start by finding the factors of 40 and 48, which are 40=1×40=1×40, 40=2×20=2×20, 40=4×10=4×10, 40=5×8=5×8, 48=1×48=1×48, 48=2×24=2×24, 48=3×16=3×16, 48=4×12=4×12, 48=6×8=6×8. \n\nThe prime factorization of 40 is 2×2×2×5=2^3×5.\nThe prime factorization of 48 is 2×2×2×2×3=2^4×3.\n\nWe now need to find the factors that both 40 and 48 share. We know that 2 is the only common factor. So, we look at the exponents of 2 in the factorizations of 40 and 48:\n\n2^3 and 2^4\n\nThe greatest common factor is the product of the lowest exponent powers of repeated factors: 2^3=8\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor of 40 and 48 is \\boxed{8}.",
